From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucaszhongsj <lucaszhongsj@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:46:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ios: a portrait pad of the ABXY reach, its own size per
 device

The portrait split had its controls at half the size of the overlay's: the
unit was taken from the band's width, which a standing phone's narrow
band made small. The unit now comes from the gap between the two rows of
controls, so every device gets the largest size its rows allow, and the
D-pad reaches as far as the ABXY diamond's keys (50 + 27 x 1.25), the
two reading as one size.

The rows sit at 50 % and 80 % of the band's safe part and the columns at
25 % and 75 %, so the lower row stays clear of the home indicator. The
L3 and R3 keys move to the line between the shoulders, as the rest of the
controls keep their own places.

The gap between two shapes is measured between their edges now, not by
growing one of them: the old way gave two answers for the same pair, and
the arrangement accepted a placement that the check then refused.

The enlarged hit targets are back to what they were: a face key reaches
the midpoint between two keys (both count there) but never a neighbour's
centre, and a shoulder or stick click answers a third beyond its drawn
key, so the target is a comfortable 44 points without the artwork
growing.

The frame-rate counter takes the gamepad's own unit, so it sits under
the menu gear at the distance the gear's radius sets.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: a portrait pad of the size its own screen allows, its D-pad at the ABXY reach, its hit targets back to a full 44 points
Issue: none yet: no upstream issue for the companion

